WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.940 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  this is rupture farms  [Music]  these working conditions may seem  harrowing but one blue-skinned mu Dakin  slave named Abe still thinks he has a  pretty good job but after stumbling upon  a rupture farms plans for a tasty new  product Abe abandons his cleaning duties  and sets out to escape the  slaughterhouse so begins Oddworld new n  tasty a remake of 1997 side-scrolling  platformer odd world Abe's Oddysee  but we're not talking about simply  upscaling the original games  pre-rendered 2d graphics no the entire  game has been rebuilt from the ground up  in real-time 3d while Abe's Oddysee  divided its levels into still screens  new and tasties camera Scrolls with a v'  as he walks runs and sneaks through odd  world  it's a thrill to see areas from Abe's  Oddysee that would have required  travelling across seven or so screens  rendered in new and tasty with an  impressive seamlessness this new camera  is also free to give a better look at  the consistently gorgeous environmental  design which has lost none of the  original games style and detail in the  move to 3d for me it felt like new and  tasty presented a literal depiction of  odd world as my mind's eye saw it in  1997 despite the new visuals new and  tasty takes great care to retain the  core side-scrolling platformer that  distinguished Abe's Oddysee 17 years ago  apes a weakling he's extremely fragile  and lacking in offensive capabilities  he's more concerned with surviving his  enemies and destroying them and he does  this by sneaking past them outrunning  them  or turning the environment on them when  possible Abe can hide in steam vents  lead gun-toting guards into landmines  zap them by activating electric fields  and occasionally he can possess a guard  to temporarily turn his gun on his  comrades Abe's enemies are scary  powerful and they exhibit unique  identities possessing a slick guard lets  you order slugs to kill another guard  para mites won't attack unless you back  them into a corner scrubs will attack on  sight unless they see another scrap in  which case the two will ignore you and  to fight to the death  exploiting these behaviors is the key to  solving most puzzles this mixes well  with the environmental hazards in ways  that never feel repetitive but Abe's  quest isn't solely about  self-preservation along the way he must  free his enslaved human brothers by  issuing them basic commands and leading  them to portals  for all the traumatic ways that Abe can  die in this hostile world there's a  slapstick quality to the dark subject  matter when you have multiple frail Mew  Dawkins in tow the variety of dialogue  in new and tasty has been greatly  increased over the original game so the  Mew Dawkins feel less like carbon copies  of one another and ragdoll physics make  everything funnier trying to survive as  a fragile character like Abe was  something of a novelty when Abe's  Oddysee was first released he died in  one hit but he had unlimited lives the  same is true of new and tasty but this  remake adds three difficulty levels the  easier of which lets you take more than  one hit before dying but even the  classic one hit kill difficulty level is  still forgiving as you can quick save by  simply tapping the touchpad keep this in  mind and you'll rarely lose much  progress from what is sure to be  repeated deaths unfortunately those  deaths sometimes occur because of how  new and tasty uses the analog stick for  movement in the original game you  control Dave's movement speed by holding  down the shoulder buttons this was  important because the game required  precise timing of Sprint's and jumps to  avoid landing on mines or falling down  chasms new and tasty changes this by  putting 2 movement speeds on the left  thumbstick pushing it slightly will make  a walk while pushing it harder will make  him run this led to a number of  situations where I had to adjust my  position by a single step but I ended up  running straight into a landmine  thankfully sneaking is still bound to a  shoulder button so it's rare that you'll  accidentally wake up a Slig and get shot  despite occasional frustrations from  this fiddly analog move  and some fourth wall breaking ingame ads  this is a remake that feels as though it  was crafted with love and respect with  clever puzzles near identical to the  original game and beautiful environments  brought to life with new visuals in a  dynamic camera new and tasty thoroughly  satiated me despite my being an oddball  the veteran and knowing each solution  and secret area like the back of my head  [Music]

